WEBVTT

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:06.256
One, two! One, two, three!

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.077
- Guidance system?
- Online.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.537
- Autopilot?
- Present.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.998
- Dark matter indicator?
- Making a noise.

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:42.792
All systems operational. Let's rock.

00:00:57.205 --> 00:00:59.582
Gentlemen, I've completed
my report on the crash.

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:04.314
Whoa! I'm not readin' that crap!
Summarize it in one word.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.690
Sabotage.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:08.902
This is a normal L-unit. Without it,

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:11.780
space travel is but
the fevered dream of a madman.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.198
- Yeah.
- Of course!

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:15.992
- It's an important unit.
- And this, my friends,

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.703
is the L-unit I just
removed from the ship.

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:24.000
That doesn't look like an "L"
at all, unless you count lowercase.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.919
- You know we don't!
- Ooh!

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:30.590
Whoever did this was strong.
This is 340 pounds of Tonka-tough steel.

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:32.842
Mmm... It should look like this...

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:36.012
But instead it looks like this.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:39.683
- Who would do a thing like that?
- Who could do a thing like that?

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.393
And by "that," I mean this.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:46.690
Well, gang, it looks like we have
another mystery on our hands.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.900
I'd better make a chart of the suspects.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:52.153
I'll begin by drawing a line
with my straightedge.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.073
Sweet lamprey of Santa Fe!

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:56.991
My edge has been bent!

00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:01.371
My javelin, too! It's ruined!

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.708
Now we'll never beat Jupiter State.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.462
My Slinky! My cuddly little pet Slinky!

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.009
What's all the hubbub?

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:17.387
My God! Even the professor's been bent!

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:21.433
Thank you for your sympathy,
talking square of linoleum.

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:22.642
I'll get you fixed up.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.478
That's fine.

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:29.357
Wait a minute! Bender,
what did you just do to the professor?

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:30.442
I bent him.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.894
- It's Bender!
- J'accusé.

00:02:32.978 --> 00:02:35.855
Oh, I see, a bunch of stuff gets bent,

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:38.525
so it must be the robot
designed for bending.

00:02:38.608 --> 00:02:39.943
I know how to settle this.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.278
We'll check last night's
surveillance tapes.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.488
- Surveillance?
- What tapes?

00:02:43.571 --> 00:02:44.572
You've seen me naked?

00:02:48.493 --> 00:02:52.205
Ah, last night's tape. It was right next
to Bathroom Bloopers Four.

00:02:59.921 --> 00:03:03.091
See? Nothin'. Told you, losers!

00:03:03.174 --> 00:03:05.969
Wait. There on the screen.
It's that guy you are!

00:03:06.094 --> 00:03:07.846
I'm sleepwalkin'.

00:03:07.929 --> 00:03:10.932
Dear Lord, we've got robots
on the ceiling!

00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:38.168
You weren't sleepwalking.
You were sleep-bending.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.711
This is quite a shock!

00:03:39.794 --> 00:03:42.839
On the other hand,
it's not surprising in the least.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:47.636
After all, I've been bending
since the day I was built.

00:03:48.219 --> 00:03:53.099
I was born on an assembly line
in the bad part of Tijuana.

00:03:56.311 --> 00:03:57.312
Mama.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:20.835
Hooray! I graduated!

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:23.421
Time to bend around Europe
for a few months,

00:04:23.505 --> 00:04:25.799
then get a job bending.

00:04:25.882 --> 00:04:27.759
You remember your own birth?

00:04:27.842 --> 00:04:29.719
Sure. It was only four years ago.

00:04:29.844 --> 00:04:33.765
- You're only four years old?
- Precocious little scamp, ain't I?

00:04:37.018 --> 00:04:38.937
Bender must have a pent-up need to bend

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.065
that's not being satisfied
by his bend-free lifestyle.

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.775
Then he can't stay here.

00:04:43.858 --> 00:04:46.653
He's a menace to every
straight person in the company.

00:04:47.529 --> 00:04:49.781
Go satisfy your bend lust,

00:04:49.864 --> 00:04:53.243
and don't you come back
to work until you do!

00:04:54.119 --> 00:04:56.788
No more bending! No more work!

00:04:56.871 --> 00:04:59.291
Give us a raise, you big fat jerk!

00:04:59.374 --> 00:05:00.375
Nevers!

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.672
Yo! The mafia supports ya!

00:05:05.755 --> 00:05:08.675
But don't tell no one. Spread the word.

00:05:08.758 --> 00:05:11.678
As the duly elected mobsters
of this union,

00:05:11.761 --> 00:05:15.515
it's our duty to support the struggle
of these proud, lazy slobs.

00:05:15.598 --> 00:05:18.268
Yeah, but what if management
remains "intragnizent"?

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.979
From the context,
it is clear what you mean.

00:05:21.062 --> 00:05:24.065
In that case, Clamps may have
a little surprise for them.

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:26.901
The clamps! Right?

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.242
Ah, no. A strike?

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.620
Now I'll never get to bend anything!

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.706
- Oh, woe is Bender!
- Hang tough, brother.

00:05:39.789 --> 00:05:43.293
Management refused our demand
to switch casual Friday to Monday.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.629
- What?
- And now they're hiring scabs

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.297
at 10 times the normal wage.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:51.885
Ten times normal wage!
I'll give those jerks what for!

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:59.476
- Welcomes aboard, scab.
- Great to be here.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:02.354
Come on. I'll introduces you
to your scab coworkers

00:06:02.437 --> 00:06:03.980
you'll be scabbin' with.

00:06:05.148 --> 00:06:07.442
This here's our scab foreman.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:10.362
- Flexo?
- Bender?

00:06:10.445 --> 00:06:13.657
Hey, sorry you got sent to that
South American Turkish prison

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.034
instead of me
on account of mistaken identity.

00:06:16.117 --> 00:06:18.036
You bastard!

00:06:18.119 --> 00:06:21.539
They treated me like an animal!
And that's what I became!

00:06:21.623 --> 00:06:26.127
Nah, you're all right.
Good to see ya, buddy.

00:06:26.211 --> 00:06:29.047
And here's another scab
what also works here.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.340
Angelyne.

00:06:34.511 --> 00:06:35.887
Hello!

00:06:37.347 --> 00:06:40.141
Hey! Youse guyses wanna move that thing?

00:06:45.522 --> 00:06:46.773
Hello!

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.864
Give us a raise, you big fat jerk!

00:06:54.948 --> 00:06:55.991
Nevers!

00:07:08.878 --> 00:07:10.171
Ow!

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:16.720
Um, hi, Angelyne. Whatcha up to?

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:20.432
Makin' hangers. Guidance counselor
said I had a knack for it.

00:07:20.515 --> 00:07:22.267
That's cool. That's cool.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.102
So, um... Uh...

00:07:24.352 --> 00:07:27.314
I was wonderin' if,
you know, it's cool if not...

00:07:27.397 --> 00:07:29.733
But what are you doin' after work?

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:32.444
What I always do. Jack squat.

00:07:32.527 --> 00:07:34.821
Me, too.

00:07:34.904 --> 00:07:36.698
Man, we have a lot in common, huh?

00:07:36.781 --> 00:07:40.118
Well, we are made of
virtually identical components.

00:07:40.201 --> 00:07:41.453
Are you sure?

00:07:41.536 --> 00:07:44.664
Maybe I should sneak a peak
at your access panel.

00:07:44.748 --> 00:07:46.833
Hey, according to the Scab Handbook,

00:07:46.916 --> 00:07:49.252
that's extremely inappropriate banter.

00:07:49.919 --> 00:07:51.713
And that's just the way I like it.

00:07:57.177 --> 00:07:59.638
Haile H. Selassie!

00:07:59.721 --> 00:08:02.849
There, little friend. Good as new.

00:08:09.022 --> 00:08:11.191
What an exquisite day!

00:08:11.274 --> 00:08:15.111
That azure sky. The verdant treetops.

00:08:15.195 --> 00:08:18.698
Those delightful birds
with their chirp, chirp, chirp

00:08:18.782 --> 00:08:21.034
and their tweet, tweet, splat.

00:08:21.117 --> 00:08:23.161
Professor, I've never
seen you so cheerful.

00:08:23.244 --> 00:08:24.829
- What the hell's wrong with you?
- Hmm...

00:08:24.996 --> 00:08:26.623
I'm not quite sure.

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:29.209
Perhaps seeing things
from a new perspective

00:08:29.292 --> 00:08:31.252
has reminded me of life's beauty.

00:08:31.378 --> 00:08:34.422
Or perhaps my new posture is causing blood

00:08:34.506 --> 00:08:36.341
to pool in the back of my brain,

00:08:36.424 --> 00:08:39.219
resulting in a mild delirium.

00:08:39.302 --> 00:08:42.305
Incidentally, you have
a dime up your nose.

00:08:42.389 --> 00:08:44.516
I wish. It's a nickel.

00:08:45.767 --> 00:08:47.227
Union forever!

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:51.272
Lousy scabs!
They can't do those things! Et cetera!

00:08:54.943 --> 00:08:58.947
I bet watchin' me bend girders
like this turns your legs all rubbery.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.157
Well, my legs are made of rubber.

00:09:01.241 --> 00:09:04.744
And anyway, I am just
as strong as you are, Mac.

00:09:04.828 --> 00:09:07.122
Oh, yeah? Prove it.

00:09:15.088 --> 00:09:17.299
Here, let me help you.

00:09:41.698 --> 00:09:45.452
Bend me, shape me
any way you want me

00:09:45.535 --> 00:09:49.122
Long as you love me, it's all right

00:09:49.205 --> 00:09:53.084
Bend me, shape me
any way you want me

00:09:53.168 --> 00:09:58.381
You got the power to turn on the light

00:09:58.465 --> 00:10:02.594
Bend me, shape me
any way you want me

00:10:02.677 --> 00:10:06.389
Long as you love me, it's all right

00:10:06.473 --> 00:10:10.226
Bend me, shape me
any way you want me

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.104
Long as you love me, it's all right

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.692
Bend me, shape me
any way you want me

00:10:20.737 --> 00:10:24.658
My new bent outlook
has completely re-energized me.

00:10:24.741 --> 00:10:28.161
I'm even dating a young
Brazilian retired actress.

00:10:28.244 --> 00:10:29.454
- Way to go!
- Great!

00:10:29.537 --> 00:10:31.831
Some say I'm robbing the cradle,

00:10:31.915 --> 00:10:34.834
but I say she's robbing the grave.

00:10:34.918 --> 00:10:37.295
Howdy, doodies! What's new?

00:10:40.548 --> 00:10:43.343
I was just regaling your former co-workers

00:10:43.426 --> 00:10:46.304
with a tale of bedroom antics
the likes of which...

00:10:46.388 --> 00:10:48.223
Yeah, yeah, big whoop. No one cares.

00:10:48.306 --> 00:10:51.643
I got Bender-related news. I'm in love.

00:10:51.726 --> 00:10:54.062
And I'm takin' all my friends
out to celebrate.

00:10:54.145 --> 00:10:56.272
Let's go live it up!

00:11:01.945 --> 00:11:06.032
Hey, look at this crowd.
You guys gotta try the pasta.

00:11:06.116 --> 00:11:08.410
It's got a real nice profit margin.

00:11:08.493 --> 00:11:10.829
Bam! So, special occasion tonight?

00:11:10.912 --> 00:11:13.790
Oh, Elzar, you'll never guess
what's happened!

00:11:13.915 --> 00:11:17.210
- Bam?
- I've met the most dynamite ladybot.

00:11:17.294 --> 00:11:19.129
Hey, that's terrific.

00:11:19.212 --> 00:11:21.715
To celebrate,
I'm gonna stick seven copies

00:11:21.798 --> 00:11:23.883
of my latest cookbook on your bill.

00:11:23.967 --> 00:11:25.677
Bless you, sir.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.556
So, Bender, tell us about
this new girlfriend of yours.

00:11:29.639 --> 00:11:32.600
I intend to,
through the lost art of the toast.

00:11:33.518 --> 00:11:36.229
To Angelyne, she's got it all.

00:11:36.313 --> 00:11:40.692
Looks, charm and the love
of a fabulous bending robot.

00:11:40.775 --> 00:11:42.527
She sure does.

00:11:47.741 --> 00:11:49.492
Flexo!

00:11:52.704 --> 00:11:54.914
Careful! That's a week old!

00:12:02.547 --> 00:12:05.091
I finally meet a nice girl,
with a pair of legs

00:12:05.175 --> 00:12:06.968
that don't quit unexpectedly,

00:12:07.052 --> 00:12:09.846
and that jerk Flexo steals her away?

00:12:09.929 --> 00:12:12.724
It's time to kick some shiny metal ass!

00:12:14.225 --> 00:12:16.394
You degenerate hussy!

00:12:16.478 --> 00:12:18.730
I'm disappointed in you too, Angelyne.

00:12:18.813 --> 00:12:21.107
Bender,
it's not what you think.

00:12:21.191 --> 00:12:23.860
Oh, God, then it's worse than I think!

00:12:23.943 --> 00:12:26.946
Now look, there is no reason to be upset.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:30.325
- Flexo and I are divorced.
- Huh?

00:12:30.408 --> 00:12:33.078
We're just havin' dinner
'cause we wanna stay friends.

00:12:33.161 --> 00:12:35.121
I knew that.

00:12:35.205 --> 00:12:38.333
What I'm actually outraged by
is your choice of wine!

00:12:38.416 --> 00:12:41.002
Really, it's the steward's fault.

00:12:41.086 --> 00:12:42.963
Excellent choice, sir.

00:12:44.589 --> 00:12:47.926
That Flexo! Why,
I'm knockin' him right on his butt.

00:12:48.009 --> 00:12:49.803
Can't believe this.

00:12:49.886 --> 00:12:51.805
Obsessing won't help, Bender.

00:12:51.888 --> 00:12:54.474
Take a lean back and enjoy life.

00:12:54.557 --> 00:12:58.144
I can't. My fembot may be
in love with another manbot.

00:12:58.228 --> 00:12:59.437
Well, talk to her.

00:12:59.521 --> 00:13:02.482
Tell her about your feelings
in an open and honest way.

00:13:02.565 --> 00:13:04.609
Yeah. Either that or be a man.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.904
Okay, I've constructed
an elaborate lie.

00:13:07.988 --> 00:13:11.324
I'll call Angelyne
while pretending to be Flexo,

00:13:11.408 --> 00:13:14.035
arrange a date, show up disguised as him

00:13:14.119 --> 00:13:16.246
and catch her two-timing me with myself.

00:13:16.329 --> 00:13:17.998
That's thinkin' like a man.

00:13:21.334 --> 00:13:25.088
Hello? This is Flexo.

00:13:35.056 --> 00:13:37.600
Now we'll see who loves whom.

00:13:47.027 --> 00:13:50.280
- Hey, hot stuff.
- Hey, Flexo.

00:13:50.363 --> 00:13:53.950
So since when do you go to bars
on work nights?

00:13:54.034 --> 00:13:55.452
It's not like you at all.

00:13:55.535 --> 00:13:57.829
Nonsense. It's exactly like me.

00:13:57.912 --> 00:14:02.709
Flexo, the fun-lovin' love machine
fembots love to love.

00:14:02.792 --> 00:14:05.045
Hey, barkeep, I'll have a fuzzy navel,

00:14:05.128 --> 00:14:07.714
and she'll have
the girliest drink in the house.

00:14:07.797 --> 00:14:09.549
Two fuzzy navels comin' up.

00:14:09.633 --> 00:14:12.344
I hope they can make change for a fortune.

00:14:13.474 --> 00:14:17.265
Yo, get an eyeload of that
filthy scab with the beard

00:14:17.349 --> 00:14:19.392
flashin' his filthy scab money.

00:14:19.476 --> 00:14:21.895
- It's an insult to you, boss.
- Yeah.

00:14:21.978 --> 00:14:25.732
That cash ought to be slushin' my fund
and kicks-in' my back.

00:14:25.815 --> 00:14:27.275
I'm greasin' up my whoozits.

00:14:27.359 --> 00:14:30.862
Whoa, whoa. Clamps. Not yet.
Let's just keep an eye on him

00:14:30.945 --> 00:14:33.323
and see if he does it a couple more times.

00:14:33.406 --> 00:14:35.659
You're looking good to Flexo tonight.

00:14:35.742 --> 00:14:37.285
Quit makin' with the googly eyes.

00:14:37.369 --> 00:14:39.162
You know that I'm in love with Bender.

00:14:39.245 --> 00:14:41.748
Bender? That walkin' wuss factory?

00:14:41.831 --> 00:14:45.377
He may be a walkin' factory,
but believe me, he is no wuss.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.128
Now look, you and me are through.

00:14:47.212 --> 00:14:49.297
I told you that when I divorced you.

00:14:49.381 --> 00:14:51.257
But goin' through a divorce together,

00:14:51.341 --> 00:14:53.927
you can't tell me
that didn't bring us closer.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.428
Care to dance?

00:14:55.512 --> 00:14:58.598
Well, you know I love dancin',
but you always hated it.

00:14:58.682 --> 00:15:01.309
In that case, it's somethin' I've always

00:15:01.393 --> 00:15:03.269
wanted to make up to you.

00:15:08.233 --> 00:15:09.609
Hey, Scratchmo!

00:15:09.693 --> 00:15:11.194
How about droppin' me and the lady

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:13.321
some rump-rattlin' beats?

00:15:13.405 --> 00:15:15.907
I had hoped by the second time
he flashed his cash,

00:15:15.991 --> 00:15:17.909
my rage would've subsided.

00:15:17.993 --> 00:15:19.995
Sadly, that has not happened.

00:15:24.249 --> 00:15:27.210
You used to be so inflexible, Flexo.

00:15:27.294 --> 00:15:29.129
You have really loosened up.

00:15:29.212 --> 00:15:31.548
I recently upgraded my funk card.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:33.591
Argh. Come on!

00:15:34.092 --> 00:15:37.345
- All right!
- Come on, now!

00:15:37.429 --> 00:15:39.014
What's new?

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.691
Flexo? What's goin' on?

00:15:50.108 --> 00:15:52.193
Did... Um...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.361
Oh!

00:15:54.154 --> 00:15:56.114
Flexo!

00:16:07.417 --> 00:16:09.836
So the moral of the story is,

00:16:09.919 --> 00:16:12.964
if you want it to stay sunk,
tie a weight to it!

00:16:15.425 --> 00:16:18.720
You know, you always were
a kick in the teeth, man.

00:16:18.803 --> 00:16:23.141
Aw, shucks, thunder buns.
You make me feel like a million volts.

00:16:23.224 --> 00:16:26.144
Oh, Flexo, Flexo, Flexo.

00:16:26.227 --> 00:16:29.356
I'm startin' to remember
why I fell for you in the first place.

00:16:29.439 --> 00:16:33.026
So, she's fallin' for Flexo, eh?

00:16:33.109 --> 00:16:36.780
I'd better seduce her
a little more, just to be sure.

00:16:36.863 --> 00:16:40.408
Well, it's late.
I should get home to my trailer.

00:16:40.492 --> 00:16:41.618
I'll walk you out.

00:16:41.701 --> 00:16:45.372
After all, a true gentlemen
tends to his date's every need.

00:16:45.455 --> 00:16:46.915
Tiparillo?

00:16:50.835 --> 00:16:52.629
Here you are, my lad.

00:16:52.712 --> 00:16:56.925
Bring the lady's car around
in the finest way possible.

00:16:57.258 --> 00:16:59.636
He's flashin' his cash loaf again.

00:16:59.719 --> 00:17:01.262
How many times is that?

00:17:01.346 --> 00:17:02.806
- Two or three?
- Three.

00:17:02.889 --> 00:17:06.017
All right. That's the necessary
number of times.

00:17:06.101 --> 00:17:09.646
That scab's gonna have a little
on-the-job accident.

00:17:09.729 --> 00:17:11.773
With all due respect, Donbot,

00:17:11.856 --> 00:17:14.401
I don't think we should rely
on an accident happenin'.

00:17:14.484 --> 00:17:15.819
Let's kill him ourselves.

00:17:17.278 --> 00:17:21.199
Well, good night. I had a great time.

00:17:21.282 --> 00:17:24.244
How about a lift to your place?

00:17:24.327 --> 00:17:26.162
- What?
- Admit it.

00:17:26.246 --> 00:17:28.164
You felt somethin' for me tonight.

00:17:28.248 --> 00:17:30.834
And by "me," I mean Flexo.

00:17:30.917 --> 00:17:32.752
Hey, look, I had fun, but...

00:17:32.836 --> 00:17:34.838
- But?
- But...

00:17:34.921 --> 00:17:38.466
But?

00:17:40.343 --> 00:17:41.344
But...

00:17:51.187 --> 00:17:54.566
Huh? Bender! You tricked me!

00:17:54.649 --> 00:17:58.445
That's right, baby!
I ain't your lover boy Flexo,

00:17:58.528 --> 00:18:00.447
the guy you love so much!

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:03.074
You even love anybody
pretending to be him!

00:18:03.158 --> 00:18:04.409
Well, maybe I love you so much,

00:18:04.492 --> 00:18:06.911
I love you no matter
who you're pretending to be.

00:18:06.995 --> 00:18:11.124
Oh, how I wish I could believe
or understand that!

00:18:11.207 --> 00:18:13.627
There's only one reasonable
course of action now.

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.253
Kill Flexo!

00:18:15.795 --> 00:18:16.796
Ow!

00:18:18.256 --> 00:18:20.759
No!

00:18:29.893 --> 00:18:31.645
Thanks. I appreciate that.

00:18:31.728 --> 00:18:34.773
Nah, I'm joshin' ya.
That was quite annoying.

00:18:34.856 --> 00:18:36.524
You call yourself divorced?

00:18:36.608 --> 00:18:39.569
You're makin' a mockery of one
of our oldest institutions!

00:18:39.653 --> 00:18:40.654
What?

00:18:44.908 --> 00:18:46.952
All right, boss. Give the word,

00:18:47.035 --> 00:18:49.204
and I'll drop this unbendable girder,

00:18:49.287 --> 00:18:50.664
clamp, clamp, ca-bamp!

00:18:50.747 --> 00:18:53.667
Remember, only kill
the one with the beard.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:56.378
That other filthy scab,
we got nothin' against.

00:19:06.054 --> 00:19:10.475
- That's low!
- Please stop! I'm not worth it!

00:19:10.558 --> 00:19:12.769
Probably not, but I love you,

00:19:12.852 --> 00:19:15.271
and I'm gonna kick his ass
till I win you back!

00:19:19.484 --> 00:19:20.485
Hey!

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:23.113
Okay, Clamps, now.

00:19:24.864 --> 00:19:26.116
Ahhh!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:29.202
Ooh, that's gotta clamp!

00:19:30.954 --> 00:19:32.747
Flexo, are you okay?

00:19:32.831 --> 00:19:34.666
Yeah. Never better.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:39.170
Nah, I'm yankin' your chain. I'm dyin'.

00:19:39.254 --> 00:19:43.341
You can't die! Tonight Bender
showed me that I love you.

00:19:43.425 --> 00:19:45.677
But... I love you.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.680
I know, and I care for you, too.

00:19:48.763 --> 00:19:50.265
But I could never love anyone

00:19:50.348 --> 00:19:53.393
as much as you made me realize
I love Flexo!

00:19:55.228 --> 00:19:58.231
But... But...

00:20:00.233 --> 00:20:02.027
I love you so much, Angelyne,

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:04.696
I want you to be happy, no matter what.

00:20:04.779 --> 00:20:06.865
But what are you sayin'?

00:20:06.948 --> 00:20:11.578
I'm sayin' I've got
an unbendable girder to bend.

00:20:12.495 --> 00:20:14.998
You can't bend that girder.
It's unbendable!

00:20:15.081 --> 00:20:17.208
Well, I don't know anything about lifting,

00:20:17.292 --> 00:20:19.461
so that just leaves us the one option.

00:20:45.862 --> 00:20:47.113
Thanks, buddy.

00:20:47.197 --> 00:20:49.699
Another year under that,
and I'd have been a goner.

00:20:50.283 --> 00:20:52.869
I'll always
remember this, Bender.

00:20:54.913 --> 00:20:57.832
Me, too. Me, too.

00:20:58.792 --> 00:20:59.918
Jerk.

00:21:02.504 --> 00:21:06.675
So, Flexo and Angelyne had sex
right there on the factory floor?

00:21:06.758 --> 00:21:09.260
Well, at least you got
bending out of your system.

00:21:09.344 --> 00:21:14.599
Yes. I won't be up to bending
again for a long, long time.

00:21:14.683 --> 00:21:17.602
Perhaps it's your outlook
that needs a good bend,

00:21:17.686 --> 00:21:19.229
a 90-degree bend

00:21:19.312 --> 00:21:23.274
to a place where happiness
is perpendicular to wonderment.

00:21:23.358 --> 00:21:25.652
Professor, we're all sick
of your upbeat attitude.

00:21:25.735 --> 00:21:26.736
- I'll say.
- Believe it.

00:21:26.861 --> 00:21:30.532
Nonsense. It's just like
in the song I wrote.

00:21:30.615 --> 00:21:33.743
We all need
a new angle on life...

00:21:33.827 --> 00:21:36.246
Bender, you've gotta help us.

00:21:36.329 --> 00:21:40.208
I try to get out,
but they keep pullin' me back in!

00:21:40.292 --> 00:21:42.544
Wangle a new dangle on life

00:21:44.129 --> 00:21:46.339
No, Bender! The other way!

00:21:46.423 --> 00:21:47.966
I like him better this way.

00:21:48.049 --> 00:21:50.218
I'm sad now.

00:21:50.302 --> 00:21:52.262
Eh, it's fine.